# Nornir cron schedule — TEMPLATE, never the live job list.
# Copy to YOUR home and edit there:  cp config/cron.yaml.example $YMIR_HOME/config/cron.yaml
# The runtime reads the operator's own schedule from $YMIR_HOME/config/cron.yaml
# (or BROKK_CONFIG_OVERRIDE) — the tracked tree ships only this shape.
# Format: HH:MM <command>. Started idempotently by bin/time/nornir-cron-start.sh.
#
# ROLE GATE (plan 51): prefix a job with @<role>[,<role>] so it runs only on the
# machines whose roles match — @heart (the record), @forge (models/GPU),
# @dev (a full body), @hand. No gate means any role. A dev body must NOT run the
# record jobs; that is how 8 orphan seat schedulers came to run a heart's work.
#   @heart 07:00 bin/time/nornir-job-daily-briefing.sh
#   07:30 bin/nornir-job-ungated.sh        # any role
#
# GATE EVERY LINE THAT BELONGS TO A ROLE. An ungated machine job runs on EVERY
# seat of every machine, so with N sessions on one box it fires N times a day
# (2026-09-28: five seats ran the machine's whole crontab, so the same briefing
# and snapshot went off five times). The list below is the shape to follow: the
# record belongs to the heart, the model work to the forge, and a full body keeps
# the supervision it alone performs.

@heart 07:00 bin/time/nornir-job-daily-briefing.sh
@heart 06:00 bin/time/nornir-job-observer.sh
@heart 08:00 bin/time/nornir-job-hall-snapshot.sh
@heart 02:30 bin/time/nornir-job-nsr-compliance.sh
@forge 00:30 bin/time/nornir-job-skillopt-sleep.sh
@heart 00:15 bin/time/nornir-job-memory-housekeeping.sh
@heart 00:00 bin/time/nornir-job-git-sync.sh
# Eir checks every surface daily (P8) — a desktop that cannot open is reported.
@heart 08:15 bin/time/nornir-job-doctor.sh
# The rollover backstop: hand off every repository that carries a .asken state,
# so a session that died without a reporter still leaves a fresh HANDOFF.md.
@heart 04:00 bin/time/nornir-job-asken-handoff.sh
